          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "まとまる — matomaru — \"to be settled; to come together\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "いけんが まとまったら、ていあんして ください。 — iken ga matomattara, teian shite kudasai — \"Once your ideas come together, please make a proposal.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Polite まとまります, matomarimasu; a godan verb. Past (polite): いけんが まとまりました。, iken ga matomarimashita."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "まとまる (matomaru) is a native Japanese word (wago), inherited rather than borrowed from Chinese, and its older origin is not settled. JMdict notes that it is usually written in kana (JMdict)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
